    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_bureaucracy_rights_eligibility",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "The rejection notice states the outcome but does not explain which eligibility requirement the application failed to meet."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "نامه رد نتیجه رو می‌گه ولی توضیح نمی‌ده درخواست کدوم شرط احراز رو نداشته."
        },
        "intent": "identify_missing_reason",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_eligibility",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_requirement",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_decision"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_bureaucracy_rights_procedure",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "I would first confirm the formal procedure, because an informal complaint may not pause the appeal deadline."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "اول رویه رسمی رو تأیید می‌کنم چون شکایت غیررسمی ممکنه مهلت اعتراض رو متوقف نکنه."
        },
        "intent": "clarify_procedure",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_procedure",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_appeal",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_deadline"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_bureaucracy_rights_evidence",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "The new evidence is relevant because it addresses the specific reason given for the decision, not merely the overall situation."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "مدرک جدید مرتبطه چون دقیقاً دلیل تصمیم رو هدف می‌گیره، نه فقط وضعیت کلی رو."
        },
        "intent": "link_evidence_to_decision",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_evidence",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_decision"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_bureaucracy_rights_review",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "I am requesting a review of the decision on the basis that the submitted document appears not to have been considered."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "درخواست بازبینی تصمیم رو دارم چون به نظر میاد مدرک ارسال‌شده بررسی نشده."
        },
        "intent": "request_review",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_review",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_decision",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_evidence"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_bureaucracy_rights_deadline",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "If the deadline cannot be extended, I would like written confirmation of the date and the acceptable submission methods."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "اگر مهلت قابل تمدید نیست، تأیید کتبی تاریخ و روش‌های قابل قبول ارسال رو می‌خوام."
        },
        "intent": "protect_deadline",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_deadline",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_procedure"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_bureaucracy_rights_requirement",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "A requirement should be applied consistently; if an exception exists, the basis for that exception should also be clear."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "یک الزام باید یکدست اعمال بشه؛ اگر استثنا وجود داره مبناش هم باید روشن باشه."
        },
        "intent": "question_consistency",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_requirement",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_eligibility"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_bureaucracy_rights_appeal",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "An appeal is more effective when it identifies the alleged error precisely rather than simply restating dissatisfaction with the outcome."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "اعتراض وقتی مؤثرتره که خطای ادعایی رو دقیق مشخص کنه، نه اینکه فقط نارضایتی از نتیجه رو تکرار کنه."
        },
        "intent": "structure_appeal",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_appeal",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_decision"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_bureaucracy_rights_close",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "My immediate goal is to preserve the right to review while gathering the strongest evidence for the substantive case."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "هدف فوری من حفظ حق بازبینیه، در حالی که قوی‌ترین مدارک برای اصل پرونده رو جمع می‌کنم."
        },
        "intent": "preserve_rights",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_review",
          "c1_bureaucracy_rights_evidence"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_bureaucracy_rights_formal_subjunctive",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-01",
        "slug": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-formal-subjunctive",
        "title": "Formal mandative structures",
        "rule_summary": "In formal recommendations and requirements, use structures such as it is essential that ... be and they recommended that ... be.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در توصیه‌ها و الزامات رسمی می‌توان از ساختارهایی مثل it is essential that ... be و they recommended that ... be استفاده کرد."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "It is essential that every applicant be given the same information.",
            "fa": "ضروری است به هر متقاضی اطلاعات یکسان داده شود."
          },
          {
            "en": "The committee recommended that the proposal be revised.",
            "fa": "کمیته توصیه کرد پیشنهاد بازبینی شود."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_bureaucracy_rights_advanced_passive",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-02",
        "slug": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-advanced-passive",
        "title": "Advanced passive choices",
        "rule_summary": "Use passive forms, including get-passives and passive infinitives, when agency is unknown, sensitive, obvious, or less important than the process.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "وقتی انجام‌دهنده نامعلوم، حساس، بدیهی یا کم‌اهمیت‌تر از فرایند است از شکل‌های پیشرفته مجهول، از جمله get-passive و passive infinitive استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Several applications appear to have been rejected automatically.",
            "fa": "به نظر می‌رسد چند درخواست به‌صورت خودکار رد شده‌اند."
          },
          {
            "en": "The issue needs to be addressed before launch.",
            "fa": "این مسئله باید قبل از عرضه رسیدگی شود."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_bureaucracy_rights_nominalisation",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-03",
        "slug": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-nominalisation",
        "title": "Nominalisation in formal discourse",
        "rule_summary": "Turn verbs or adjectives into noun phrases to make formal arguments more compact and abstract when appropriate.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در گفتار و نوشتار رسمی، در صورت مناسب بودن فعل یا صفت را به عبارت اسمی تبدیل می‌کنیم تا استدلال فشرده‌تر و انتزاعی‌تر شود."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The rapid expansion of the service created new risks.",
            "fa": "گسترش سریع سرویس ریسک‌های جدیدی ایجاد کرد."
          },
          {
            "en": "A reduction in waiting times would benefit everyone.",
            "fa": "کاهش زمان انتظار به نفع همه خواهد بود."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_bureaucracy_rights_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-bureaucracy-rights-01",
        "title": "Bureaucracy & Rights: part 1",
        "setting": "strategy meeting",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "requests",
        "characters": [
          "Mei",
          "Omar"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Mei",
            "text": "What do you make of the way this is being framed?",
            "translation_fa": "از نحوه مطرح شدن این موضوع چه برداشتی داری؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
